control-pane proximity: uncommitted edits are invisible (git diff base...HEAD sees only commits)

Agent proximity only sees **committed** work. `runGitDiff` diffs `<base>...HEAD`, so a session's staged and unstaged edits are invisible. Two agents editing the same lines get no advisory until both have committed, which is the very window proximity is meant to cover.

**Version.** `main` at ef648e0, Linux x86_64, Node 22.23.3, git 2.x. The older commit ccc1fd0 behaves the same.

**Repro.** Save as `repro-proximity.js` in the repo root and run `node repro-proximity.js`. It needs `git` on PATH, and builds a throwaway repo with two worktrees in the OS temp directory:

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const os = require('os');
const path = require('path');
const { execFileSync } = require('child_process');
const { buildProximitySnapshot } = require('./scripts/lib/control-pane/proximity');

const git = (cwd, ...args) => execFileSync('git', ['-C', cwd, ...args], { stdio: 'pipe' });
const repo = path.join(fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'ecc-prox-')), 'repo');
fs.mkdirSync(path.join(repo, 'src'), { recursive: true });
git(repo, 'init', '-q', '-b', 'main');
git(repo, 'config', 'user.email', 'demo@example.com');
git(repo, 'config', 'user.name', 'demo');
const file = 'src/shared.js';
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, file), Array.from({ length: 40 }, (_, i) => `const line${i + 1} = ${i + 1};`).join('\n') + '\n');
git(repo, 'add', '.');
git(repo, 'commit', '-qm', 'base');
for (const name of ['a', 'b']) git(repo, 'worktree', 'add', '-q', '-b', `agent-${name}`, `${repo}-${name}`, 'main');

// Both agents edit lines 11-13 of the same file, and neither has committed yet.
for (const name of ['a', 'b']) {
  const p = path.join(`${repo}-${name}`, file);
  const lines = fs.readFileSync(p, 'utf8').split('\n');
  for (let i = 10; i <= 12; i += 1) lines[i] += ` // edited by agent ${name}`;
  fs.writeFileSync(p, lines.join('\n'));
}

const sessions = ['a', 'b'].map(name => ({ id: `sess-${name}`, task: `agent ${name}`, createdAt: new Date().toISOString(), worktree: { path: `${repo}-${name}`, branch: `agent-${name}`, base: 'main' } }));
const scan = () => {
  const s = buildProximitySnapshot(sessions, { repoRoot: repo });
  return { agents: s.counts.agents, advisories: s.advisories.map(a => a.level) };
};
console.log('uncommitted edits :', JSON.stringify(scan()));
for (const name of ['a', 'b']) git(`${repo}-${name}`, 'commit', '-qam', `agent ${name}`);
console.log('after both commit :', JSON.stringify(scan()));
```

Output:

```
uncommitted edits : {"agents":0,"advisories":[]}
after both commit : {"agents":2,"advisories":["resolution"]}
```

**Cause.** [proximity.js#L48-L55](https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC/blob/ef648e01899ba3e8dc6371642deaaf64b4477775/scripts/lib/control-pane/proximity.js#L48-L55) runs `git -C <worktree> diff --unified=0 <base>...HEAD`. The three-dot form compares the merge base with `HEAD`, so it covers commits only.

**Possible fix.**
- Diff the merge base against the **working tree**: `git diff --unified=0 <merge-base>`, with the merge base from `git merge-base <base> HEAD`. That covers staged and unstaged edits.
- Add `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` for new untracked files, as whole-file entries.

**Related, smaller.** The dependency channel resolves only relative specifiers ([graph.js#L26-L35](https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC/blob/ef648e01899ba3e8dc6371642deaaf64b4477775/scripts/lib/agent-proximity/graph.js#L26-L35)). In npm and pnpm workspaces, imports between workspace packages (`@scope/pkg`) are in-repo coupling, but they are dropped as node_modules. `.svelte` and `.vue` files are not scanned at all.

