## Version

deno 2.9.5 (stable, release, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu)
v8 15.0.245.2-rusty
typescript 6.0.3

## Steps to reproduce

1. Create file `test.js` with the following content:
```js
const dns = require('node:dns');

const host = "www.iana.org";

try {
    dns.resolveAny(host, (err, records) => {
    if (err) 
        console.log({ ok: false, info: err });
    else 
        console.log({ ok: true, info: `records=${records}` });
    });
} 
catch (e) {
    console.log(`Exception thrown: ${e.stack}`);
}
```
2. Run the file like `deno -A test.js`.

## Expected Behaviour
Node.js prints:
```js
{
  ok: true,
  info: 'records=[object Object],[object Object],[object Object],[object Object],[object Object],[object Object],[object Object],[object Object]'
}
```

## Actual Behaviour
Deno prints:
```js
{
  ok: false,
  info: Error: queryAny UNKNOWN www.google.com
      at QueryReqWrap.onresolve [as oncomplete] (ext:deno_node/dns.ts:1:3606)
      at ext:deno_node/internal_binding/cares_wrap.ts:1:3996 {
